WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.667 --> 00:00:03.067
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show," everybody.

00:00:03.067 --> 00:00:04.067
You're here.
You made it.

00:00:04.067 --> 00:00:05.334
Thank you for watching at home.

00:00:05.334 --> 00:00:06.501
Thank you for being here.

00:00:06.501 --> 00:00:09.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:09.767 --> 00:00:12.067
You guys
ready to talk elections?

00:00:12.067 --> 00:00:13.300
-Yeah!
-Yeah!

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:15.734
-What a great topic, yeah.

00:00:15.734 --> 00:00:19.767
Republicans didn't win enough,
Democrats didn't lose as much.

00:00:19.767 --> 00:00:22.801
Everyone was walking the streets
today like, "Are you happy?"

00:00:22.801 --> 00:00:24.167
[ Laughter ]
"Are you happy?

00:00:24.167 --> 00:00:25.434
Are we happy?"

00:00:25.434 --> 00:00:28.133
Yep, the country is finally
united under, "Eh."

00:00:28.133 --> 00:00:30.100
[ Laughter ]

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:31.367
It was a strange night.

00:00:31.367 --> 00:00:33.167
It's not often you hear
somebody excitedly say,

00:00:33.167 --> 00:00:35.200
"It's okay!
We only lost the House."

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:36.701
[ Laughter ]

00:00:36.701 --> 00:00:39.601
For both parties, it wasn't
great, but also not terrible.

00:00:39.601 --> 00:00:42.467
It was the political version
of eating at TGI Fridays.

00:00:42.467 --> 00:00:44.801
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.801 --> 00:00:46.834
So in the end,
Republicans could get the House,

00:00:46.834 --> 00:00:48.567
Democrats could hold the Senate,

00:00:48.567 --> 00:00:50.968
and your Thanksgiving dinner
will still be a disaster.

00:00:50.968 --> 00:00:52.000
[ Laughter ]

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:53.467
As of now,
there's still some races

00:00:53.467 --> 00:00:54.868
that are still
too close to call,

00:00:54.868 --> 00:00:58.334
but according to the media,
there was one clear loser.

00:00:58.334 --> 00:01:00.334
-It's a bad, bad night
for Donald Trump.

00:01:00.334 --> 00:01:01.634
-Very bad night
for Donald Trump.

00:01:01.634 --> 00:01:02.868
-It is bad night for Trump.

00:01:02.868 --> 00:01:04.767
-What I can tell you is,
the biggest loser

00:01:04.767 --> 00:01:06.901
tonight is Donald Trump.

00:01:06.901 --> 00:01:09.133
-Donald Trump was
the biggest loser of the night.

00:01:09.133 --> 00:01:11.767
-He's the biggest loser
in American politics.

00:01:11.767 --> 00:01:13.300
-Donald Trump's
not gonna like this.

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:15.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:17.300
-Wow.

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:19.300
Trump was so mad,
he ran upstairs

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:21.300
and slammed the door
of his tanning bed.

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.067
[ Laughter ]

00:01:24.067 --> 00:01:25.534
Ketchup everywhere.

00:01:25.534 --> 00:01:26.934
[ Laughter ]

00:01:26.934 --> 00:01:29.367
Well, one of the most talked
about races was in Pennsylvania,

00:01:29.367 --> 00:01:32.701
where John Fetterman was able
to defeat Dr. Oz.

00:01:32.701 --> 00:01:36.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:36.067 --> 00:01:38.300
Basically, people
hit the voting booth, saw Oz,

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:40.834
and then paid no attention
to the man behind the curtain.

00:01:40.834 --> 00:01:42.767
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.767 --> 00:01:44.567
Dr. Oz knew he was in trouble

00:01:44.567 --> 00:01:46.200
when his own neighbors
didn't vote for him.

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:48.701
Yeah, they said, "We couldn't.
We live in New Jersey."

00:01:48.701 --> 00:01:51.067
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.067 --> 00:01:53.167
And get this,
apparently Trump blamed Melania

00:01:53.167 --> 00:01:55.400
for convincing him
to back Dr. Oz,

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:59.033
saying that it wasn't
her best decision.

00:01:59.033 --> 00:02:01.734
Then Melania was like, "Well,
it certainly wasn't my worst."

00:02:01.734 --> 00:02:04.701
[ Laughter and applause ]
-Oh! Oh!

00:02:04.701 --> 00:02:08.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:08.801 --> 00:02:11.033
-Yep, news networks
are still analyzing

00:02:11.033 --> 00:02:12.968
John Fetterman's victory,
which brings us

00:02:12.968 --> 00:02:14.767
to our newest segment,
"Can't Argue With That."

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:15.767
Here we go.

00:02:15.767 --> 00:02:18.501
♪♪

00:02:18.501 --> 00:02:20.667
-Why did Dr. Oz lose?

00:02:20.667 --> 00:02:24.000
Well, it looks like,
according to the exit polling,

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:25.834
it's because Fetterman won.

00:02:25.834 --> 00:02:28.434
♪♪

00:02:28.434 --> 00:02:30.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:30.267 --> 00:02:33.067
♪♪

00:02:33.067 --> 00:02:35.300
-Sure.
-[ Laughing ]

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:38.067
-Meanwhile, down in Florida,
Governor Ron DeSantis

00:02:38.067 --> 00:02:40.868
was re-elected by a huge margin,
and a lot of people are saying

00:02:40.868 --> 00:02:44.234
it makes him the Republican
front runner for 2024.

00:02:44.234 --> 00:02:46.067
Which is surprising --
-Whoo!

00:02:46.067 --> 00:02:48.200
-Which is surprising
'cause it's hard to run anywhere

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:49.434
in those boots.

00:02:49.434 --> 00:02:53.601
[ Laughter ]

00:02:53.601 --> 00:02:55.467
Some other races
people are talking about,

00:02:55.467 --> 00:02:58.167
a 25-year-old
named Maxwell Frost

00:02:58.167 --> 00:03:00.701
was elected as the first gen Z
member of Congress.

00:03:00.701 --> 00:03:04.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:04.767 --> 00:03:06.734
Yep.
He was the only winner

00:03:06.734 --> 00:03:09.934
to begin a victory speech with,
"Well, this low-key slaps."

00:03:09.934 --> 00:03:15.300
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:17.100
Of course,
it's a huge celebration

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:18.901
for the candidates who win,

00:03:18.901 --> 00:03:20.367
but it's sad
for the ones who lose

00:03:20.367 --> 00:03:22.901
because they still
set up a party.

00:03:22.901 --> 00:03:25.534
Take a look
at Doug Mastriano's party

00:03:25.534 --> 00:03:27.267
after he lost the Pennsylvania
governor's race.

00:03:27.267 --> 00:03:28.267
Look at this.

00:03:28.267 --> 00:03:30.200
-♪ The Vengabus is coming ♪

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:31.701
♪ And everybody's jumping ♪

00:03:31.701 --> 00:03:33.501
♪ New York to San Francisco ♪
-That's sad.

00:03:33.501 --> 00:03:35.167
♪ An intercity disco ♪
[ Laughter ]

00:03:35.167 --> 00:03:37.968
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:37.968 --> 00:03:39.767
You know it's a tough night
when the dance floor

00:03:39.767 --> 00:03:41.067
looks like a still photo.

00:03:41.067 --> 00:03:43.067
Do you know what I'm saying?
[ Laughter ]

00:03:43.067 --> 00:03:45.601
I'm not sure what the energy
of an election party should be,

00:03:45.601 --> 00:03:46.834
but it's definitely not

00:03:46.834 --> 00:03:48.767
"wedding reception
that just had a fistfight."

00:03:48.767 --> 00:03:50.200
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:52.300
Yeah, the midterms are over,
and there are winners,

00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:53.434
and obviously, there are losers

00:03:53.434 --> 00:03:55.300
who have to make
a concession speech,

00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:57.033
so as a service,
we thought we'd help them out

00:03:57.033 --> 00:03:59.033
by giving them some lines
that they can use

00:03:59.033 --> 00:04:01.400
to start off
those concession speeches.

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:02.734
For instance, there's...

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:06.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:06.934 --> 00:04:10.334
"Gotta pay for that.
Gotta pay for that."

00:04:10.334 --> 00:04:12.000
Next, there's...

00:04:15.067 --> 00:04:18.100
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:20.734
"You want to chitchat or no?
Okay."

00:04:20.734 --> 00:04:22.400
Next, there's...

00:04:24.601 --> 00:04:29.067
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:29.067 --> 00:04:30.734
Next there's...

00:04:33.167 --> 00:04:37.734
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:37.734 --> 00:04:39.767
Well, this one's short.
Next, there's...

00:04:41.601 --> 00:04:46.133
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:46.133 --> 00:04:47.634
And finally...

00:04:49.767 --> 00:04:51.100
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:56.601
They just got to own it.
They just got to own it.

00:04:56.601 --> 00:04:59.000
Well, it's the day after
the midterms with a lot

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:00.834
of big races
still too close to call,

00:05:00.834 --> 00:05:03.400
and you could tell the networks
are trying to fill time

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:06.501
'cause this is what you see
right now when you turn on CNN.

00:05:06.501 --> 00:05:16.467
-Breaaaaaaaaaaaakiiiiiiiiiing...

00:05:16.467 --> 00:05:17.234
[ Breathes deeply ]

00:05:17.234 --> 00:05:18.701
News.

00:05:18.701 --> 00:05:19.968
-Still nothing.

00:05:19.968 --> 00:05:22.367
-There you go.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:22.367 --> 00:05:27.801
Still nothing.
[ Applause ]

00:05:27.801 --> 00:05:29.467
Switching gears,
some entertainment news --

00:05:29.467 --> 00:05:33.033
I read that Netflix wants
to start offering live sports.

00:05:33.033 --> 00:05:35.634
Yep. There will be
way fewer penalties in football

00:05:35.634 --> 00:05:37.367
when this is the referee.

00:05:37.367 --> 00:05:40.400
Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:41.934
Well, you guys, earlier tonight

00:05:41.934 --> 00:05:43.767
was the annual
Country Music Awards.

00:05:43.767 --> 00:05:46.467
I love the CMAs,
but I gotta say,

00:05:46.467 --> 00:05:48.467
I didn't know a lot
of this year's performers.

00:05:48.467 --> 00:05:50.267
Take a look.
Maybe you'll agree.

00:05:50.267 --> 00:05:51.868
-The CMAs would like to thank

00:05:51.868 --> 00:05:53.133
all the of
the amazing performers

00:05:53.133 --> 00:05:55.801
at tonight's incredible
ceremony, including...

00:06:15.834 --> 00:06:17.434
And Carrie Underwood.

00:06:17.434 --> 00:06:19.267
-Yeah, well,
I know Carrie Underwood.

00:06:19.267 --> 00:06:24.701
I know...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:24.701 --> 00:06:26.501
Did you guys see this?
A man in the U.K.

00:06:26.501 --> 00:06:29.734
was just arrested for allegedly
throwing eggs at King Charles.

00:06:29.734 --> 00:06:31.067
[ Laughter ]

00:06:31.067 --> 00:06:33.033
Yep, some of the eggs
shattered on the ground.

00:06:33.033 --> 00:06:35.167
And this is tragic,
but it's been reported that

00:06:35.167 --> 00:06:37.667
all the King's horses
and all the King's men...

00:06:37.667 --> 00:06:39.000
[ Laughter ]

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:41.300
...couldn't put them back
together again.

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:46.901
[ Laughter ]

00:06:46.901 --> 00:06:50.267
Guys, listen to this.
A Southwest Airlines pilot

00:06:50.267 --> 00:06:52.601
proposed to his girlfriend
over the P.A. system

00:06:52.601 --> 00:06:54.367
during a flight.

00:06:54.367 --> 00:06:55.868
Yep, then
the flight attendant was like,

00:06:55.868 --> 00:06:57.434
"If you want to say no,
the emergency exits

00:06:57.434 --> 00:07:01.100
are located here and here."
[ Laughter ]

00:07:01.100 --> 00:07:03.300
And, finally, it is Wednesday,
and we all know what that means.

00:07:03.300 --> 00:07:04.801
It's time for some
"Monday Motivations."

00:07:04.801 --> 00:07:05.801
Here we go.

00:07:05.801 --> 00:07:06.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:06.934 --> 00:07:12.367
♪♪

00:07:12.367 --> 00:07:15.133
You're so popular,
when someone says November,

00:07:15.133 --> 00:07:18.200
everyone else is like, "Oh, you
mean McKenzie's birthday month?"

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:21.400
[ Applause ]

00:07:21.400 --> 00:07:23.200
After they welcome you
onto the flight,

00:07:23.200 --> 00:07:25.367
the pilots go into the cockpit,
shut the door behind them,

00:07:25.367 --> 00:07:26.634
and go, "Oh, my God,
he's here.

00:07:26.634 --> 00:07:27.734
Be cool, be cool."

00:07:27.734 --> 00:07:31.167
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:31.167 --> 00:07:33.100
No matter what you went as
for Halloween,

00:07:33.100 --> 00:07:35.567
people assumed
you were the sexy version.

00:07:35.567 --> 00:07:39.400
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:39.400 --> 00:07:41.100
Go ahead, say you're vegan.

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:42.234
People care.

00:07:42.234 --> 00:07:46.167
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:46.167 --> 00:07:48.300
When you read on the subway,
everyone's like,

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:50.234
"Oh, he's the full package."

00:07:50.234 --> 00:07:53.801
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:53.801 --> 00:07:56.367
If you'd been on stage
that night, John Wilkes Booth

00:07:56.367 --> 00:07:57.767
would've been like,
"Forget Abe Lincoln.

00:07:57.767 --> 00:07:59.467
I want to see
the rest of this play."

00:07:59.467 --> 00:08:02.701
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:02.701 --> 00:08:04.701
And finally, this year,
your uncle's gonna show up

00:08:04.701 --> 00:08:06.934
to Thanksgiving like,
"I've given it some thought,

00:08:06.934 --> 00:08:08.901
and I realize, you're right."

00:08:08.901 --> 00:08:09.934
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:09.934 --> 00:08:10.934
There you go.
Thank you.

00:08:10.934 --> 00:08:12.167
We have a great show, everyone.

00:08:12.167 --> 00:08:14.968
Octavia Spencer is here tonight!

00:08:14.968 --> 00:08:17.934
[ Cheers and applause ]
Octavia!

00:08:17.934 --> 00:08:20.534
Matthias Schweighofer
is on the show!

00:08:20.534 --> 00:08:21.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:21.834 --> 00:08:23.567
And we've got great stand-up
from Kurt Braunohler.

00:08:23.567 --> 00:08:24.801
Stick around.

00:08:24.801 --> 00:08:26.801
We're playing "Catchphrase"
when we come back.

